# Ticket 34: exceptions for the CI `trivy` job's image vulnerability scan
# (https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore).
#
# The scan already skips vulnerabilities with no fix available, so an entry
# here is a reviewed decision to ship a fixable one for now. Every entry needs
# a comment above it giving the reason, and an `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` expiry on the
# ID's line. Trivy enforces the expiry: once it passes, the finding fails the
# scan again, so the exception is reviewed rather than kept by accident.
#
# Example:
#   # <package> <version>: only reachable via <feature>, which we don't use;
#   # fix lands in the next base-image digest bump
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
